  beta @ n_samples=2000   (their default): -0.6721
  beta @ n_samples=200000 (100x finer):    -0.6721
  |delta beta| = 0.0000   worst peak miss = 0.051%

  => PUBLISHED -0.672 IS SOUND. At t_max=12 the sampling is adequate:
     the enstrophy peak is broad on that horizon. The defect is a LATENT
     FRAGILITY -- it bites whenever t_max grows (or the peak sharpens),
     because the sampling interval t_max/n_samples is not tied to the
     feature being measured. Fix: track a running max of the per-step
     `current_enstrophy` already computed for the ceiling test.
